    "['local-user [parameter1] password irreversible-cipher [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user authentication encrypted-password \"@%@%UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC:@%@%\"', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the specified HUAWEI command:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user authentication encrypted-password \"@%@%UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC:@%@%\"\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. In Juniper:\\n   - `class super-user` provides equivalent privileges to HUAWEI\\'s privilege level 3\\n   - The encrypted password format is preserved as-is\\n   - Juniper automatically handles the \"irreversible-cipher\" aspect when using the encrypted-password option\\n2. The SSH service configuration would need additional Juniper-specific commands (not shown here) to fully match the HUAWEI configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user authentication encrypted-password \"@%@%UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC:@%@%\"'}]]": 1,
    "['local-user [parameter1] privilege level [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for `local-user client001 privilege level 3`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\n##\\n\\nThe `super-user` class in Juniper is equivalent to privilege level 3 (administrative/root level access) in Huawei\\'s implementation. This command sets the user \"client001\" to have the highest privilege level on the Juniper device.', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user'}]]": 1,
    "['local-user [parameter1] service-type [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper command for the HUAWEI `local-user client001 service-type ssh` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\nset system services ssh root-login deny\\nset system services ssh protocol-version v2\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 mapping for \"service-type ssh\" since it handles authentication methods differently.\\n2. The above commands:\\n   - Set the user class to super-user (equivalent to privilege level 3)\\n   - Configure SSH to use password authentication\\n   - Deny root login (security best practice)\\n   - Force SSH protocol version 2\\n3. The actual password would be set separately with `set system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password`', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh authentication-order password', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper command for the HUAWEI `local-user client001 service-type ssh` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\nset system services ssh root-login deny\\nset system services ssh protocol-version v2\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 mapping for \"service-type ssh\" since it handles authentication methods differently.\\n2. The above commands:\\n   - Set the user class to super-user (equivalent to privilege level 3)\\n   - Configure SSH to use password authentication\\n   - Deny root login (security best practice)\\n   - Force SSH protocol version 2\\n3. The actual password would be set separately with `set system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password`', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh authentication-order password'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh root-login deny', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper command for the HUAWEI `local-user client001 service-type ssh` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\nset system services ssh root-login deny\\nset system services ssh protocol-version v2\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 mapping for \"service-type ssh\" since it handles authentication methods differently.\\n2. The above commands:\\n   - Set the user class to super-user (equivalent to privilege level 3)\\n   - Configure SSH to use password authentication\\n   - Deny root login (security best practice)\\n   - Force SSH protocol version 2\\n3. The actual password would be set separately with `set system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password`', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh root-login deny'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh protocol-version v2', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper command for the HUAWEI `local-user client001 service-type ssh` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\nset system services ssh root-login deny\\nset system services ssh protocol-version v2\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 mapping for \"service-type ssh\" since it handles authentication methods differently.\\n2. The above commands:\\n   - Set the user class to super-user (equivalent to privilege level 3)\\n   - Configure SSH to use password authentication\\n   - Deny root login (security best practice)\\n   - Force SSH protocol version 2\\n3. The actual password would be set separately with `set system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password`', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh protocol-version v2'}]]": 1,
    "['local-user [parameter1] password irreversible-cipher [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client002 class super-user authentication encrypted-password \"<password_for_client002>\"', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the specified HUAWEI command:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client002 class super-user authentication encrypted-password \"<password_for_client002>\"\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. In Juniper:\\n   - `super-user` maps to privilege level 3 (highest privileges)\\n   - `encrypted-password` is the equivalent of `irreversible-cipher`\\n   - Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct service-type parameter like HUAWEI, but the SSH access would be controlled by the overall system services configuration\\n\\n2. The actual encrypted password string would need to be replaced with a properly hashed Juniper-compatible password (Juniper uses a different hashing algorithm than HUAWEI)', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client002 class super-user authentication encrypted-password \"<password_for_client002>\"'}]]": 1,
    "['local-user [parameter1] privilege level [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client002 class super-user', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client002 class super-user\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `local-user` is equivalent to creating a login user under `system login user`.\\n- `privilege level 3` maps to Juniper\\'s `super-user` class, which provides the highest privilege level (equivalent to level 3 in Huawei).\\n- The command sets the user \"client002\" with super-user privileges (level 3 equivalent).\\n- Note that Juniper doesn\\'t use numeric privilege levels like Huawei; instead, it uses predefined classes (super-user, operator, etc.).', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client002 class super-user'}]]": 1,
    "['local-user [parameter1] service-type [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client002 class super-user', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `local-user client002 service-type ssh`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client002 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\nset system services ssh user-authentication order password\\nset system services ssh user-authentication password\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 mapping for Huawei\\'s \"service-type ssh\" concept\\n2. The translation involves:\\n   - Setting the user class to super-user (equivalent to privilege level 3)\\n   - Configuring SSH password authentication\\n   - Enabling password authentication for the user\\n3. In Juniper, SSH access is implicitly enabled when you configure user authentication methods', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client002 class super-user'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh authentication-order password', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `local-user client002 service-type ssh`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client002 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\nset system services ssh user-authentication order password\\nset system services ssh user-authentication password\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 mapping for Huawei\\'s \"service-type ssh\" concept\\n2. The translation involves:\\n   - Setting the user class to super-user (equivalent to privilege level 3)\\n   - Configuring SSH password authentication\\n   - Enabling password authentication for the user\\n3. In Juniper, SSH access is implicitly enabled when you configure user authentication methods', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh authentication-order password'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh user-authentication order password', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `local-user client002 service-type ssh`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client002 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\nset system services ssh user-authentication order password\\nset system services ssh user-authentication password\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 mapping for Huawei\\'s \"service-type ssh\" concept\\n2. The translation involves:\\n   - Setting the user class to super-user (equivalent to privilege level 3)\\n   - Configuring SSH password authentication\\n   - Enabling password authentication for the user\\n3. In Juniper, SSH access is implicitly enabled when you configure user authentication methods', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh user-authentication order password'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh user-authentication password', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `local-user client002 service-type ssh`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client002 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\nset system services ssh user-authentication order password\\nset system services ssh user-authentication password\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 mapping for Huawei\\'s \"service-type ssh\" concept\\n2. The translation involves:\\n   - Setting the user class to super-user (equivalent to privilege level 3)\\n   - Configuring SSH password authentication\\n   - Enabling password authentication for the user\\n3. In Juniper, SSH access is implicitly enabled when you configure user authentication methods', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh user-authentication password'}]]": 1,
